  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 217 PM CDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\nFriday the ridge looks to migrate ever so slowly eastward and be \npositioned over west TX also weakening in the process. However we \narent expecting temperatures nearly as hot as this past weekend as \nthis ridge should be weaker aloft. Additionally, we could see our \ntypical seabreeze kick off showers and storms across the Coastal \nPlains due to this weaker ridge located overhead. \n\nThis weekend is when things get a bit more tricky as the ridge will \nbe continuing its progression eastward but flattening/broadening out \nas it does so. Models are struggling on the placement of this ridge \nas they typically do in weaker scenarios thus we still are expecting \nhot temperatures however they should be closer to around 100 \ndegrees. This weaker ridge may get interrupted by a disturbance \nmoving towards the Gulf coast starting early next week. This may \nbring back some low rain chances to the area and also help keep \nhighs below Heat Advisory levels. Similarly the afternoon seabreeze \nshould help to kick off isolated showers and a few rumbles of \nthunder across the Coastal plains as we resume our typical summer \npattern. Stay tuned.",
